# __DISPLAY_NAME__

This project was created with `create-natui-app`.

## Run in development

NatUI requires Node.js 22 or newer.

```bash
__INSTALL_COMMAND__
__RUN_COMMAND__ dev
```

The first launch downloads the prebuilt native host for the installed NatUI
release and caches it per user; later launches start from that cache. Run
`npx natui host install` to download it ahead of time, or set `NATUI_HOST` to
a self-built host executable from the
[NatUI framework repository](https://github.com/floklein/natui).

The development server watches `src/main.tsx` and applies React Fast Refresh
to the existing native window.

## Application configuration

`natui.app.json` contains the application identity, source entry, output
directory, and platform icon paths. The generated icon files use native
container formats:

- `assets/AppIcon.icns` for macOS
- `assets/AppIcon.ico` with multiple resolutions for Windows

Replace both files with your final application artwork before distribution.
Keep the configured file formats, use complete PNG or JPEG 2000
representations inside the macOS `.icns`, and
include the platform-recommended sizes.

`@natui/core` does not include native host sources, so standalone projects
cannot package a native artifact yet. The configuration is ready for the
packager in a NatUI framework repository checkout.
